# Flutter Desktop Rules

## 1. Platform Adaptation

- Use `Theme.of(context).platform` to detect the running platform.
- Material 3 as baseline. Cupertino styling for macOS-specific widgets (buttons, dialogs, nav).
- `defaultTargetPlatform` for platform-specific behavior in tests.
- Avoid platform-conditional imports. Use `dart:io` Platform check + service abstraction instead.

## 2. Window Management

- `WindowManager` from `window_manager` package: set size, position, minimum constraints.
- Listen to `windowManager.addListener` for resize/move events — update layout accordingly.
- Multiple windows: `desktop_multi_window` package. Each window has its own controller.
- Save/restore window position to `shared_preferences`.

## 3. Platform Channels (MethodChannel / Pigeon)

- Define API contracts with `pigeon` → generates typed host+client code.
- One `MethodChannel` per feature domain (e.g., `com.myapp.notifications`, `com.myapp.filesystem`).
- Handle `MissingPluginException` gracefully — user may be on unsupported platform.
- All platform channel calls must have timeout + fallback.

## 4. Menu Bar & System Tray

- `MenuBar` widget for native macOS menu bar (`PlatformMenuBar` for Windows fallback).
- System tray: `system_tray` package with `initSystemTray()` and menu items.
- Keyboard shortcuts: `Shortcuts` + `Intent` with platform-appropriate key bindings (Cmd on macOS, Ctrl on Windows).

## 5. File System & Dialogs

- `file_picker` for open dialogs. `path_provider` for app directories.
- `save_file_dialog` from `file_picker` for save-as workflows.
- App data: `getApplicationSupportDirectory()` for SQLite/drift databases.
- Never hardcode paths. Always use `path_provider` APIs.

## 6. Packaging & Distribution

- Build: `flutter build macos --release` / `flutter build windows --release` / `flutter build linux --release`.
- Package: `flutter_distributor` for .dmg (macOS), .msi (Windows), .deb/.AppImage (Linux).
- macOS signing: configure `macos/Runner/DebugProfile.entitlements` and `Release.entitlements`.
- Windows signing: integrate `signtool` via `flutter_distributor` config.
- Linux: Flathub compatible Flatpak manifest via `flutter_distributor package --format flatpak`.

## 7. Auto-Update

- `shorebird` for Flutter code push — over-the-air updates for Dart code.
- `sparkle_flutter` for macOS full binary updates.
- Windows: MSIX automatic updates via Microsoft Store or custom updater.
- Linux: Flathub handles updates automatically.
